<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman starts Dead Sea.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman starts Dead Sea.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dead Sea Works Ltd, an Israel-based producer of potash, chlorine and other materials from the Dead Sea, was rated &quot;neutral&quot; as Lehman Brothers started coverage of the stock, the investment bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Lehman analyst Elise Horowitz said the company, 89 percent owned by Israel Chemicals Ltd, was fully valued at 21.3 times expected earnings for 1997.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
